  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off scheduled for June 15th. The initial budget was $500,000, but it was later adjusted to $550,000 to cover unforeseen expenses and integrate real-time analytics. The project has progressed through several phases: the design phase was completed, followed by the development phase led by Omar Jensen. A strategic partnership with TechInnovate was established to support AI research goals. The team expanded by adding five members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with an onboarding session on September 10th. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the achievement of the first major milestone ahead of schedule, involving a successfully tested prototype for secure file sharing. The next phase involves user interface enhancements planned for October, followed by security protocol updates (multi-factor authentication and encryption) effective January next year. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November. Celebrations for the testing milestone are scheduled for October 10th."
